mod:store_holder_with_refs;
// Landing 177d2b7, row 4 (DEF-591's `dw_rw1`, direction Wc): a store through a chain ref whose holder HOLDS the indirection's pointee is a store into that
// holder with refs too, as `rrti_path` asks it, of every root but a `pick` binding (`rrti_chain`'s `rrti_is_target`). A local struct holding a getter's
// pointer (`SLV:s = SLV{ l: raw getownv(hp), z: 1i64 }`) and a replacement through it (`<-(s.l) = raw mkv(h2)`) stored `h2` into the parameter's own `List`
// with nothing in the summary, so the caller's pointer into the replaced buffer read freed heap. One site per face closed here, each a fault on main
// (78f9b3a): `dw_rw1`, and seven spellings of it from W2's attack: one struct deeper (`c_nest`), in a `loop` (`c_loop`), under an `if` (`c_br`), through
// casts (`c_cast`), a value from a `pick` (`c_pickv`), through a struct copy (`c_copy`) and in an array of pointers (`c_arr`).
// Each cell's declarations carry its name as a suffix, and its `main` is `cell_main_<name>`. The controls that run are in
// tests/backend/programs/store_holder_with_refs_ok.npk.
// PRICES: the two cells marked PRICE below are right programs this row's text refuses, each failing closed, at parity: each one's by-name twin, the next
// cell, is refused by main (78f9b3a) at the same site.
error:E5;
